# The spack CPU target every image build pins, per CPU family (uname -m): a portable baseline
# rather than the build node's own microarchitecture, so one image runs on every CPU of the family
# that postdates the baseline. Host detection bakes in the build node's ISA, and the preloaded
# allocator then dies on SIGILL at container start on an older CPU.
#
# AVX-512 is used where it pays, at run time: OpenBLAS dispatches (+dynamic_dispatch), and so do MKL
# and TBLIS; code an agent compiles is built on the node itself. MPI, HDF5 and the solvers gain
# nothing from it.
#   x86_64_v3: AVX2/FMA (Haswell, Zen 1 and newer; the MI250X nodes' hosts are Zen 3)
#   armv8.2a:  Neoverse N1 and newer (Graviton 2, Altra, Grace)
SPACK_TARGET_x86_64=x86_64_v3
SPACK_TARGET_aarch64=armv8.2a
